\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Left: the 2-D toy problem. All the spread is along $x$ and all the class information along $y$, so PCA picks the useless direction (48.5\% error, chance 50\%) and Fisher the useful one (97.0\%). Right: ORL mean face, first eight eigenfaces and first eight Fisherfaces.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Yale: eigenfaces are smooth and face-like, Fisherfaces are speckled and concentrate around the eyes and brow. This is predicted, not incidental --- whitening scales each eigen-direction of $S_W$ by $1/\sqrt  \lambda $, and the small-$\lambda $ directions are the high-frequency ones.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
